{"skill":{"slug":"bbc-news","displayName":"BBC News"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1768398865276,"changelog":"Initial release: Fetch BBC News from various sections (UK, World, Business, Politics, Technology, etc.) and regions via RSS feeds. Supports text and JSON output.","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"README.md","size":1809,"sha256":"3a487ab5b2e4c147e884058d6048740bd68fe148492504cbccfcd06a2941bf63","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":2220,"sha256":"73f5bf4c9f8a3a413e7dab5156dc86fc4a8fb5251e8b5fba65eb62986ecb9dac","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/feeds.md","size":1716,"sha256":"ec9721bf248993bc372491cdaa7bd263ac6be03cf75e2be2f3418f884c99512d","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/bbc_news.py","size":5546,"sha256":"19f1bf49583cd0c8785bfce7cad531555dfc60bde0b72140e3f988485e59d1af","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1532,"sha256":"a35565aef500d4af7e2537ee346479f3cc11fed45f0b44ce0476e4058b38f1f8","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789015656428,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"94edadcb34ec5939f9f47665dbdce3e297f91246e4e549c606c25cdcbb08066f","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/94edadcb34ec5939f9f47665dbdce3e297f91246e4e549c606c25cdcbb08066f","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: bbc-news\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle is designed to fetch and display BBC News stories from RSS feeds. The `SKILL.md` provides clear instructions for the agent to execute the `scripts/bbc_news.py` script, which in turn makes HTTP GET requests exclusively to legitimate BBC RSS feed URLs (`feeds.bbci.co.uk`). There is no evidence of data exfiltration, malicious execution, persistence mechanisms, prompt injection attempts against the agent, or obfuscation. All code and documentation align with the stated purpose of providing BBC News access.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779159744029},"skillspector":{"status":"clean","normalizedStatus":"clean","score":5,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"SAFE","issueCount":1,"checkedAt":1789015656428},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This BBC News skill is a straightforward RSS reader with expected network access and only routine dependency-installation caution.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The script contacts only hard-coded HTTPS BBC RSS endpoints and does not read local files, credentials, environment variables, or user-supplied remote URLs.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"Installation uses a normal ClawHub/manual skill install path and documents pip3 install feedparser without a pinned version or hash, creating a supply-chain hardening gap but not evidence of malicious behavior.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Runtime instructions are narrow and user-invoked; the examples mention JSON output as --json in places, while the script actually implements --format json, which is a usability issue rather than a security concern.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The artifacts show no background service, scheduled task, privilege escalation, memory writes, tool hijacking, or persistence beyond installing the skill files and Python dependency.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is to fetch BBC News stories via RSS, and the shipped script does that using hard-coded BBC feed URLs and a fixed section allowlist.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Before installing, use a virtual environment if possible and consider pinning feedparser to a reviewed version. Expect the skill to make outbound HTTPS requests to BBC RSS feed URLs when you ask it for news.","findings":"[SQP-2] expected: The network fetch is expected for a BBC RSS news skill and is limited to hard-coded BBC feed URLs; adding clearer runtime disclosure would improve transparency but does not create a Review-level concern.\n[T08] expected: Using feedparser is coherent with RSS parsing, but the documented unpinned pip install should be treated as a dependency hygiene issue; there is no artifact evidence that the dependency name or install flow is deceptive.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789015656428}}}}}